# TextFSM template: Cisco IOS / IOS-XE
# `show bgp vrf <VRF> {ipv4|ipv6} unicast <prefix|community|...>` /
# `... regexp <as-path-regex>`. Shared by bgp.route / bgp.community
# / bgp.largecommunity / bgp.aspath because all four commands emit
# the same path-block shape.
#
# Canonical block (truncated):
#   BGP routing table entry for 1.1.1.0/24, version 5
#     Paths: (2 available, best #1, table default)
#     Advertised to update-groups:
#        1
#     Refresh Epoch 1
#     65001 65002
#       10.0.0.2 from 10.0.0.2 (10.0.0.2)
#         Origin IGP, metric 0, localpref 100, valid, external, best
#         Community: 65000:100 65000:200
#         Large-Community: 214503:8:3607
#         rx pathid: 0, tx pathid: 0x0
#         Updated on Aug 25 2025 16:00:00 UTC
#
# Capture strategy:
#   - The AS-path appears on its own line *before* the nexthop
#     block, as a space-separated list of ASNs. We capture the
#     full run into a single `as_path` token; the projector's
#     splitListToken() explodes it into per-ASN entries.
#   - Communities and Large-Community lines likewise use single
#     captures spanning the whole value list. Large-Community is
#     hyphenated in IOS-XE (vs `Large Community:` in EOS).
#   - `origin (\w+)` excludes the trailing comma so the wire field
#     stays `igp` / `egp` / `incomplete` rather than `igp,`.
#   - `best` is captured by a separate optional sub-pattern at the
#     end of the Origin line.
#   - `Updated on Aug 25 2025 16:00:00 UTC`-style age string
#     captured for `age` (projector best-effort; degrades to 0).
Value Filldown prefix ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+/\d+)
Value as_path (\d+(?:\s+\d+)*)
Value nexthop ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value peer_ip ([0-9a-fA-F:.]+)
Value origin (\w+)
Value med (\d+)
Value local_pref (\d+)
Value communities (\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+)*)
Value large_communities (\d+:\d+:\d+(?:\s+\d+:\d+:\d+)*)
Value best (best)
Value age (\S+\s+\S+\s+\d+\s+\d+(?:\s+\d{2}:\d{2}:\d{2})?)

Start
  ^\s*BGP routing table entry for\s+${prefix}(?:,\s+version\s+\d+)?
  ^\s+Refresh\s+Epoch\s+\d+
  ^\s+(?P<_as>${as_path})\s*$$
  ^\s+${nexthop}\s+from\s+${peer_ip}\s+\(\S+\)
  # Origin / metric / localpref / best — comma-separated. The
  # trailing `best` keyword (when present) lands on the same line,
  # after an arbitrary number of comma-separated flag tokens.
  ^\s+Origin\s+${origin}(?:,\s+metric\s+${med})?(?:,\s+localpref\s+${local_pref})?(?:,.*?${best})?\s*$$
  ^\s+Community:\s+${communities}\s*$$
  ^\s+Large-Community:\s+${large_communities}\s*$$
  ^\s+Updated\s+on\s+${age} -> Record
  ^\s*$$
